{
  "version": 2,
  "about": [
    "The production tree: every product, the workshop and station that make it, the education it needs, and its inputs.",
    "Workshops are few and broad (DF-style): each is a room type whose recipes span several tiers. A recipe runs on one of the workshop's stations (machine parts, each built in sizes 1-5), so a workshop grows with the colony by adding stations rather than new rooms.",
    "To add a product: add an item and a recipe naming an existing workshop and station. Add a station only for a genuinely new process; add a workshop only for a new trade.",
    "Education gates recipes, not rooms: a worker may run a recipe at or below their level, so one Smelter has unskilled hands at the bloomery beside Scholars at the aether furnace.",
    "Tiers are not stored: a product's tier is 1 + the highest tier among its inputs (raw = 0).",
    "Ratios are deliberately absent: an input is just an item id; counts ('logs*2') come later.",
    "Education is acyclic: each level is taught from goods made by recipes of lower levels only. Teaching a level needs a teacher of that level, so founders bring a few Literates and a Scholar; the first Magister arrives as an event once the Academy has an attunement circle.",
    "'uses' lists end uses outside the factory chain (needs, culture, construction, military, parts). Each workshop's 'later' lists products that would naturally slot in."
  ],
  "educationLevels": ["Unskilled", "Literate", "Scholar", "Magister"],
